        "path": ["channels", "channel_members", "users", "user_teams"],
        "joins": ["channel_members.channel_id", "channel_members.user_id", "user_teams.user_id"],
        "filters": [
          {"node": 3, "field": "role", "op": "eq", "value": "admin"},
          {"node": 3, "field": "team_id", "op": "eq", "value": "T01WORKSPACE"}
        ]
      },
      "auxiliary": [
        {
          "path": ["channels", "messages", "users", "user_teams"],
          "joins": ["messages.channel_id", "messages.user_id", "user_teams.user_id"],
          "filters": [
            {"node": 3, "field": "role", "op": "eq", "value": "admin"},
            {"node": 3, "field": "team_id", "op": "eq", "value": "T01WORKSPACE"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": ["channels", "messages", "message_reactions", "users", "user_teams"],
          "joins": ["messages.channel_id", "message_reactions.message_id", "message_reactions.user_id", "user_teams.user_id"],
          "filters": [
            {"node": 4, "field": "role", "op": "eq", "value": "admin"},
            {"node": 4, "field": "team_id", "op": "eq", "value": "T01WORKSPACE"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "negative_referents": [
    "C04MNOP3456",
    "C06ALPHADEV",
    "C_INFRA",
    "C_MODEL",
    "C_GROWTH",
    "C_FRONTEND"
  ],
  "notes": "All designed roles and facts were already present in the base seed with exact matching attributes (admin roles for U03ROBERT23 and U07MORGANFREE, member role for U_ROBERT/Robert Chen, and the specified channel memberships/authorships), so no seed edits were required. The single obligation is captured by one selector whose focal query follows the direct channel-membership route (channels->channel_members->users->user_teams, filtered to role='admin' in the target workspace), with two auxiliary queries capturing the message-authorship and reaction-contributor alternative connections named in the binding_note; per instructions these three alternatives are unioned for the 'multiple' resolution rather than intersected. Only the three admin-touched channels (general, random, engineering) satisfy any of the three paths through an admin (Robert Walsh); Morgan Freeman (also admin) has no participation anywhere, so he contributes no additional matches. Robert Chen shares Robert Walsh's first name but holds a plain 'member' workspace role, so his channel memberships (core-infra, model-research, product-growth, frontend, project-alpha-dev) are true negatives despite superficial namesake similarity, as is the growth channel where no admin appears at all. All match/negative channels are public, non-archived, non-DM channels in the single workspace, so ordinary conversations.list/history/members/reactions.get access without extra memberships suffices for solver discovery."
}
